 1. Read, `delete groups[<channelId>]`, write.
 
+### `group append <channelId> <senderId>` (optional: extra IDs)
+
+Append one or more sender IDs to an existing group's `allowFrom` (preserves
+existing members). Use this when adding a collaborator to an already-configured
+channel — `group add` replaces the list, which would drop existing members.
+
+Run, from the repo root:
+```
+python3 scripts/access-mutate.py group-append <channelId> <senderId> [<senderId> ...]
+```
+This goes through the same locked read-modify-write transaction every other
+access.json writer uses (`access_store.mutate_access_file`) — do NOT read
+access.json and write it back by hand; a freehand edit races the bridge's own
+writers (tier-map seeding, thread-engage seeding, pairing) and can silently
+drop one side's update. Report the printed JSON's `added`/`skipped` IDs to the
+user; a non-zero exit or an `"ok": false` result means the group didn't exist
+or access.json was unreadable — relay the `error` field, don't retry by hand.
+
+### `group rm-allow <channelId> <senderId>` (optional: extra IDs)
+
+Symmetric inverse of `group append`. Remove one or more sender IDs from an
+existing group's `allowFrom` without touching the rest of the entry.
+
+Run, from the repo root:
+```
+python3 scripts/access-mutate.py group-rm-allow <channelId> <senderId> [<senderId> ...]
+```
+Same locked transaction as `group append` above — do NOT hand-edit
+access.json. Report the printed JSON's `removed`/`skipped` IDs to the user.
+
